   "comment_0":"So basically from what I understand this is how this thing works:

The processor, has access to DDR, it is a masater to (CONV accelerator and DMA)
DMA is master  to BRAM.

So basically DMA is going to be filling BRAM, Accelerator reads from BRAM using MAC stream provider and index generator. Outputs of the MAC
get dequantized for the next layer. This cycle continues until the inference is done. At the end DMA puts the result back in DDR.",
   "comment_1":"The main memory transfer between DDR and DMA happens between CDMA's
M_AXI and PS's S_AXI_HP0 which is connected to DDR. So CDMA acts as the master
and PS/DDR act as slave. The other interface between DMA and PS where PS is
the master is for configuring the CDMA and writing to its registers.",
   "comment_2":"CDMA reads from DDR (and note that AXI has both read and write) then routes it through
the crossbar and then writes it into the BRAM.",
   "commentid":"comment_0|comment_1|comment_2|",
